        <main class="terms-content">
            <section class="terms-clause" id="acceptance"><span>01</span><div><h2>Acceptance of these terms</h2><p>By accessing or using SDUT Swap, you agree to follow these Terms of Service, the Community Guidelines, and the applicable rules of your university. If you do not agree, do not use the platform.</p><p>These terms apply to everyone using the service, including people browsing listings, creating accounts, messaging users, buying, or selling.</p></div></section>

            <section class="terms-clause" id="eligibility"><span>02</span><div><h2>Eligibility and accounts</h2><ul><li>SDUT Swap is intended for members of the university student community who are eligible to use the service.</li><li>Provide information that is accurate and keep your account details up to date.</li><li>Sellers must complete the required student identity verification before publishing listings, where that feature is required by the platform.</li><li>Maintain the security of your login credentials. You are responsible for activity carried out through your account unless applicable law provides otherwise.</li><li>Do not impersonate another person, create misleading accounts, or use another student's credentials.</li><li>Do not create multiple accounts to evade restrictions or moderation decisions.</li></ul></div></section>

            <section class="terms-clause" id="conduct"><span>03</span><div><h2>Respectful and lawful conduct</h2><p>Use SDUT Swap honestly and respectfully. You agree not to:</p><ul><li>Harass, threaten, bully, discriminate against, or intimidate another user.</li><li>Defraud, deceive, manipulate, or deliberately mislead buyers or sellers.</li><li>Send spam, repeated unwanted messages, malicious links, or harmful files.</li><li>Attempt to access another user's account or data without permission.</li><li>Interfere with the platform, bypass its security, or misuse its features.</li><li>Use the service for unlawful activity or any purpose unrelated to legitimate marketplace use.</li></ul></div></section>

            <section class="terms-clause" id="listings"><span>04</span><div><h2>Listings and prohibited items</h2><p>You are responsible for every listing you publish. Information, photos, prices, availability, and item condition must be accurate and not misleading. You must have the right to sell the item and must describe important defects honestly.</p><p>Do not list stolen, counterfeit, illegal, dangerous, or otherwise prohibited goods. Do not list items whose sale is restricted by law or university rules, including items that require a licence or authorization you do not have. The platform may remove listings that appear unsafe, unlawful, deceptive, or inconsistent with these terms.</p><p>Do not use listings to advertise unrelated services, distribute spam, or collect other users' personal information.</p></div></section>

            <section class="terms-clause" id="transactions"><span>05</span><div><h2>Transactions between users</h2><p>SDUT Swap provides a place for students to discover listings and communicate. Unless expressly stated otherwise, the platform does not own, inspect, store, ship, or sell the items listed by users and is not a party to agreements between buyers and sellers.</p><ul><li>Buyers and sellers are responsible for agreeing on the price, condition, payment method, and handover arrangements.</li><li>Buyers should inspect an item before paying and should not rely solely on listing photos or messages.</li><li>Sellers should confirm that payment has actually arrived before handing over an item.</li><li>Users should arrange exchanges in safe, public campus locations and follow the Safety Tips.</li><li>Do not assume that a listing, account, message, or payment screenshot is a guarantee of the other party's identity or performance.</li></ul><p>Any dispute about an item or payment should first be addressed directly and respectfully between the users. You may also report conduct that violates platform rules.</p></div></section>

            <section class="terms-clause" id="content"><span>06</span><div><h2>Your content and permissions</h2><p>You retain responsibility for the text, images, and other material you submit. You must have the rights and permissions needed to publish it, and it must not violate another person's privacy, intellectual property, or other rights.</p><p>By submitting content, you give SDUT Swap permission to host, display, and process that content as needed to operate, maintain, and promote the marketplace within the service. This permission is limited to those platform purposes; you remain responsible for your content.</p><p>Do not upload private documents, payment credentials, passwords, or personal information that does not need to appear in a listing.</p></div></section>

            <section class="terms-clause" id="safety"><span>07</span><div><h2>Safety, reports, and support</h2><p>Users can report listings, accounts, or conversations that appear suspicious or violate these terms. Please provide accurate details and relevant evidence when submitting a report.</p><p>Our team may review reports and take appropriate action, but we cannot guarantee that every harmful interaction or problematic listing will be detected or prevented. For immediate danger or suspected criminal activity, contact campus security or the appropriate local authorities rather than relying only on an in-platform report.</p><p>Read the <a href="/safety">Safety Tips</a> before arranging an exchange.</p></div></section>

            <section class="terms-clause" id="moderation"><span>08</span><div><h2>Moderation, removal, and suspension</h2><p>To help protect the community and maintain the service, SDUT Swap may review reported activity, remove or restrict content, limit features, or suspend accounts when there is a reasonable concern about a violation, safety risk, abuse, or legal requirement.</p><p>Where appropriate, we may consider the seriousness and context of the issue. Do not attempt to evade a restriction by creating another account. If you believe an action was taken in error, contact the Support Center and explain the situation.</p></div></section>

            <section class="terms-clause" id="availability"><span>09</span><div><h2>Platform availability and changes</h2><p>We aim to keep SDUT Swap useful and available, but we do not promise uninterrupted or error-free operation. Features may be updated, changed, temporarily unavailable, or discontinued for maintenance, security, or operational reasons.</p><p>Users should keep their own copies of important transaction information and should not rely on the platform as the only record of an agreement or payment.</p></div></section>

            <section class="terms-clause" id="liability"><span>10</span><div><h2>Disclaimers and liability</h2><p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, SDUT Swap is provided on an “as available” basis. We do not guarantee the accuracy of user listings, the quality or safety of items, another user's identity, or that a transaction will be completed successfully.</p><p>To the extent permitted by law, SDUT Swap is not responsible for losses, damage, disputes, or harm arising from interactions or transactions between users, or from interruptions to the service. Nothing in these terms excludes or limits any responsibility that cannot legally be excluded or limited.</p></div></section>

            <section class="terms-clause" id="changes"><span>11</span><div><h2>Updates to these terms</h2><p>We may revise these terms as the platform develops or when operational, safety, or legal requirements change. The updated version will be published on this page with a revised update date. Continued use after an update takes effect means you accept the revised terms, to the extent permitted by applicable law.</p></div></section>

            <section class="terms-clause" id="contact"><span>12</span><div><h2>Questions or concerns?</h2><p>If you have a question about these terms, need to report a concern, or believe an account action was made in error, contact the team through the Support Center.</p><a class="terms-contact-link" href="/support">Go to Support Center <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>
